  "id": "lens-model",
  "term": "lens model",
  "definition": "In this context, the lens model is a system-level framework for understanding deception by mapping the linked steps involved in lying and lie detection. It organizes research around choosing to lie, producing cues to deception, noticing those cues, and deciding whether someone is telling the truth.",
